Two slots suffice for these finite, one-shot processes when the marker queue has one slot and scheduling is fair. Do not infer that the same capacities suffice for every loop built around the same body. A producer permitted to start another batch before the consumer finishes the current one introduces different reachable occupancies. Analyze the loop or design a batch protocol that provides the missing bound.

